head='''# Skill-by-skill matrix — W1

Baseline: 76 active skills, at HEAD `51106e1`; six archives excluded. Every active body was inspected. See [inventory](evidence/inventory.json), [numbered complete bodies](evidence/all-active-skills-numbered.txt), and [supporting excerpts](evidence/supporting-source-numbered.txt).

**Verification limits:** “keep” means the purpose and static procedure are sound, not a measured model efficacy claim. Live triggering/efficacy for every row is **UNVERIFIED**. No paid model tasks were launched. Script/resource existence and selected adversarial paths were checked; every supporting reference's substantive correctness was not exhaustively runtime-tested. “Fix” preserves the useful skill, not archive-by-default. No skill merits archiving on present evidence; merges/splits below concern doctrine/adapter placement, not deletion of specializations.

Capabilities: R=read/search, W=write/edit, S=shell, F=web fetch/search, A=subagent, P=parallel/fresh-context reviewer, T=shared tasks/messages, C=completion gate, Q=human clarification, M=disk memory, B=visible browser, U=artifact publish, L=lifecycle hooks, N=scheduler. Body requirements may exceed allowed-tools; this is itself a portability issue. CC=Claude Code; Other=non-Claude converter path. CC “designed” is not a live host smoke. Other “blocked” means excluded from conversion, not that the host lacks equivalent capabilities. Other “degraded” includes resource/route limitations, even for portable flags.

Size column is **body words / full file lines / reference-file count**; words are NOT tokens. All active files have fewer than 500 physical lines; orchestrator is 5,463 body words. Agent Skills recommends fewer than 5,000 **tokens**, so several bodies warrant token measurement. Trigger column is static collision analysis, not precision/recall.

| Skill / category | Purpose and distinct value (overlap) | Verdict / issue | Capability dependencies | Delivery status | Trigger assessment | Size W/L/refs | Evidence / severity |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
'''
rows=[]
for x in inv:
 n=x['frontmatter']['name']; p=x['path']; purpose,overlap,trigger,issue=data[n]; cat=p.split('/')[1]; tools=x['frontmatter'].get('allowed-tools',[]); caps=['R']
 if any(t in tools for t in ['Write','Edit']): caps+=['W']
 if 'Bash' in tools:caps+=['S']
 if any(t in tools for t in ['WebFetch','WebSearch']):caps+=['F']
 if 'Agent' in tools or cat in ['loops','orchestrator']:caps+=['A','P']
 if cat in ['loops','orchestrator']:caps+=['C','M','Q']
 if n in ['babysit','dependency-health-loop','nightly-docs-and-changelog','repo-cleanup-loop','self-healing-loop']:caps+=['N']
 if n in ['orchestrator-task-loop','orchestrator']:caps+=['T','L']
 if n in ['playwright','render-sanity','frontend-agent','qe-agent','ui-brief','website-walkthrough-video','diagnose-loop','payload-cms']:caps+=['B']
 if n in ['grill-me','find-unknowns','plan-intake','setup-project-skills','settings-consolidator']:caps+=['Q']
 if n=='artifact-publish':caps+=['U']
 if n in ['llm-wiki','wiki-research','context-manager','maintain-context','living-plan']:caps+=['M']
 if n in ['class-extraction-guard','design-token-guard','prose-slop-guard','deployment-checklist']:caps+=['C']
 gated=x['frontmatter'].get('requires_claude_code',False); status='CC designed; Other blocked' if gated else 'CC/Other portable doctrine; delivery degraded'
 verdict='keep' if n in keep else 'fix'
 if n=='orchestrator':verdict='split doctrine/adapters'
 sev='P1' if gated and n not in ['settings-consolidator','use-pxpipe','artifact-publish'] else 'P2'
 if n in keep:sev='P3' if n not in ['payload-cms','yagni-gate'] else 'P2'
 ev=extra.get(n,cite(p,1)); rows.append(f'| [{n}](../../../{p}) / {cat} | {purpose}. {overlap}. | **{verdict}**: {issue}. | {", ".join(dict.fromkeys(caps))} | {status} | {trigger}. | {x["body_words"]}/{x["lines"]}/{len(x["references"])} | {ev}; full body {cite(p,20)} / **{sev}** |')
write('01-skill-matrix.md',head+'\n'.join(rows)+'''

## Resource and cross-reference resolution

[Literal resource misses](evidence/literal-resource-misses.json) are candidates, **not** 57 broken links: sibling loop references are qualified by `loop-controller`, cross-skill files by their owning skill, and root scripts explicitly by the repository. Manual refutation prevents treating those as missing resources. Actual distribution gaps remain: root catalog/health/scanner/template helpers are not bundled; flat layouts do not preserve relative resource paths; all assets and skill-creator's `agents/` / `eval-viewer/` are omitted by directory-copy conversion. See [toolchain](07-toolchain.md).

Dependency graph: contract-author → implementation roles → contract-auditor static → QE runtime → deployment-checklist. Find-unknowns before/after is not grill-me; class-extraction utility runs are not token policy; code-review Standards/Spec lanes are not security-only audit. Keep these distinctions. Prefer widening their execution modes rather than replacing them with generic “universal-agent” copies.
''')
